Test the Station in the Simulation Model
Now we are ready to test our screwdriver station in the simulation model.
• Insert a Source, which produces the pallets which we want to screw together. We named it
SourcePallets.
Insert a second Source, which feeds the screws required for screwing together the pallets. We named it
SourceScrews. We received the screw, including the JT file, from a colleague.
• Insert a Drain, which removes the finished pallets from the plant.
• Insert our Screwdriver station.
• Insert three Conveyors between the Sources, the Drain, and the Screwdriver station.
• Connect all objects with Connectors. Connect the SourcePallets, that produces the MU > PartsCarrier,
with the ConveyorPallets, and with the InterfaceInPallet of the Screwdriver. Connect the SourceScrews
that produces the MU > Screw, with the ConveyorScrews, and with the Interface named InScrew.
Connect the ConveyorOut with the Interface named Out and then with the Drain. The simulation model
should now look like this:
Test the Station in the Simulation Model
10-1048 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

You might be wondering how we inserted the Conveyors with an inclination to smoothly connect to the
Screwdriver station. We proceeded as follows:
◦ For the ConveyorPallets we entered an Anchor Point Height of 1 meter for the first anchor point
and an anchor point height of 0.15 meters for the second anchor point into the dialog Line/Arc
Parameters. This is the height of the object SourcePallets to which we connect it on the left-hand
side.
◦ For the ConveyorOut we edited values in the dialog Edit 3D Properties > Appearance. We entered a
Base Height of 0.15 meters, which means that the left-hand side of the ConveyorOut is placed 15
centimeters above the floor. We then clicked Segments and entered 1 meter as the Z dimension so
that the right-hand side connects smoothly to the Drain.
◦ When you run the simulation, you might want to run it with a low real-time factor to be able to
watch how the screwdriver actually screws the screws in.
Test the Station in the Simulation Model
Plant Simulation Help 10-1049
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

