Animate Bricks on the Animation Area of the Brick Carrier
When Plant Simulation places objects onto other objects, in our example bricks and glass bricks on the
brick carrier, it automatically distributes them evenly across the animation area of the brick carrier.
Plant Simulation distributes them according to their size and to the size and dimension of the brick
carrier.
In our example the brick carrier can accommodate 50 bricks on its animation area, each of which is 20
centimeters long and 10 centimeters wide. The brick carrier is 110 centimeters long and wide. According
to its x-dimension 5 bricks fit in a row side by side in the x-direction. According to its y-dimension 10 bricks
fit in a row in the y-direction.
Animate Bricks on the Animation Area of the Brick Carrier
Plant Simulation Help 10-1061
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

We used the default settings of the brick carrier/container.
Back to Model a Complex Receiving Department
Animate Brick Carriers on the Animation Area of the Truck
When Plant Simulation places objects onto other objects, in our case brick carriers onto the loading space,
i.e., the animation area of the truck, we would like to determine where on the bed it places the brick
carriers.
We defined animation areas for the objects with matrix loading space ParallelStation, Sorter, Store,
Transporter, and Container. These should cover your basic modeling needs.
In our case we changed the graphic of the truck, which we derived from the Transporter. We thus have to
change the animation area settings.
Proceed as follows:
Animate Brick Carriers on the Animation Area of the Truck
10-1062 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Change to the Class Library and click MUs > Truck with the right mouse button.
• Click Open In 3D.
• Click the right mouse button in the window .MUs.Truck and select Edit 3D Properties > MU
Animation.
• You can now adjust the area settings under animation area so that the brick carriers are evenly
distributed across the loading space of the truck. Plant Simulation computes the animation area of the
object as soon as you click Apply in the dialog Edit 3D Properties. The window of our partial model
then also shows these changes.
• We selected the settings above. Now everything is correct.
Animate Brick Carriers on the Animation Area of the Truck
Plant Simulation Help 10-1063
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

We can also replace the simple graphic of the truck with the graphic of the new version of Plant
Simulation.
To do so:
• Duplicate the Transporter, rename it to TruckDumper, and exchange its graphic.
• Enter the dumper as the MU to be created into the SourceTruck.
Animate Brick Carriers on the Animation Area of the Truck
10-1064 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Now only 6 brick carriers are loaded instead of the intended 8.
To fix this, increase the X-Dimension of the loading space from 3 to 4.
Animate Brick Carriers on the Animation Area of the Truck
Plant Simulation Help 10-1065
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• We finally adjust the animation area settings of the bed.
◦ Open the TruckDumper in a new window, click in the background, and press the spacebar.
◦ Activate the Animation Area [described] on the tab MU Animation and Show it.
◦ Click in the text boxes and roll the mouse wheel until the animation area has the correct size.
Animate Brick Carriers on the Animation Area of the Truck
